  "content": {
    "id": "v2-9f0a2-p19-practice-slot-7-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": null,
    "prompt": "Find the first term and the number of terms of an arithmetic series with $d=5$, $\\ell=32$ and $S_n=95$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$a=-13$, $n=10$.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}S_n&=\\frac n2(a+\\ell)\\\\95&=\\frac n2(a+32)\\\\190&=n(a+32)\\qquad\\text{(1)}\\end{align*}$$\n$$\\begin{align*}a_n&=a+(n-1)d\\\\32&=a+(n-1)(5)\\\\32&=a+5n-5\\\\a&=37-5n\\qquad\\text{(2)}\\end{align*}$$\nSubstitute (2) into (1):\n$$\\begin{align*}190&=n(37-5n+32)\\\\190&=n(69-5n)\\\\5n^2-69n+190&=0\\\\(5n-19)(n-10)&=0\\\\n&=10\\qquad(n\\text{ is a whole number})\\end{align*}$$\n$$\\begin{align*}a&=37-5(10)\\\\a&=-13\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 80
  },
